  "docs/about": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "text": "EldenNet lets characters of the game hold a free conversation with you, in their own voice, written by an AI model you choose. It reads the game and never changes it, and works only offline, alone in your own world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "table": {
          "columns": [
            {
              "id": "part",
              "label": "Part"
            },
            {
              "id": "version",
              "label": "Version"
            }
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "part": "EldenNet",
              "version": "0.1.0"
            },
            {
              "part": "GraceUI",
              "version": "0.2.12"
            },
            {
              "part": "Build",
              "version": "0.1.0"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "text": "System › Status › Compatibility says whether this version of EldenNet supports your game's build, and which GraceUI it needs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "The project",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "text": "EldenNet is free software under the MIT License, developed with AI assistance. Its engine follows the logic and structure of SkyrimNet, whose author permits EldenNet to build on it: "
          },
          {
            "doc": "licences",
            "text": "Licences and credits"
          },
          {
            "text": " gives the credit in full."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "text": "EldenNet is not affiliated with or endorsed by FromSoftware or Bandai Namco."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "See also",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "doc": "getting-started",
            "text": "Getting started"
          },
          {
            "text": " · "
          },
          {
            "doc": "licences",
            "text": "Licences and credits"
          },
          {
            "text": " · "
          },
          {
            "doc": "privacy",
            "text": "Privacy"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "About"
  },
  "docs/getting-started": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "text": "EldenNet lets characters of the game hold a conversation with you. You type a line; the character answers in their own voice, in text on screen, written by an AI model that you choose. This page takes you from a fresh install to your first conversation."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What this version does",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "list": [
          [
            {
              "text": "The characters listed on "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Characters › Named NPCs"
            },
            {
              "text": " answer when you speak to them. In this version the list is short."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Each of them has a profile EldenNet wrote in its own words, and knows what anyone would know on first meeting them. "
            },
            {
              "doc": "spoilers",
              "text": "Spoilers: how EldenNet keeps them"
            },
            {
              "text": " says more."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "You can add notes of your own on how a character speaks, on the same page under "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Your notes"
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Conversation is in text, in a box on screen. Characters only talk: they take no other action."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "EldenNet reads the game and never changes it. It writes nothing into the game, and it never edits your saves."
            }
          ]
        ],
        "ordered": false
      },
      {
        "heading": "What it does not do yet",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "list": [
          [
            {
              "text": "Other characters, soldiers and passers-by say nothing."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Characters do not speak up on their own, greet you or talk among themselves."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Nothing is remembered once the game closes. Within a session, a character recalls the last lines of your previous conversation with them."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "There are no voices: lines are text only."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Some parts of the menu have no pages yet, and are not shown."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Playing on a Steam Deck or under Proton is not covered by this version."
            }
          ]
        ],
        "ordered": false
      },
      {
        "heading": "What you need",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "list": [
          [
            {
              "text": "The game on PC, through Steam. EldenNet works only offline, alone in your own world, without Easy Anti-Cheat, and its launcher starts the game that way."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "GraceUI, the menu and on-screen layer EldenNet draws through. It comes with EldenNet."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "An AI provider. It can be a cloud service, with a key of your own from that service (which may charge for its use), or a model server on this PC, or one on another PC of your home network."
            }
          ]
        ],
        "ordered": false
      },
      {
        "heading": "Your first conversation",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "list": [
          [
            {
              "text": "Install EldenNet and GraceUI as "
            },
            {
              "doc": "installing",
              "text": "Installing and starting EldenNet, and updating GraceUI"
            },
            {
              "text": " says."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Start the game with "
            },
            {
              "code": true,
              "text": "eldennet-launcher.exe"
            },
            {
              "text": ". The first time, read the notices it shows before the game starts."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Open the menu with "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "F5"
            },
            {
              "text": ". The menu is also in your browser while the game runs: GraceUI › Browser view gives its address."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "On "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Home"
            },
            {
              "text": ", read the Status card: its State and Why rows say how EldenNet stands. It cannot read Speaking until a model answers."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "On "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "AI › Models"
            },
            {
              "text": ", choose a preset, or keep the one shown. A preset chooses a model for each job."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "On "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "AI › Providers"
            },
            {
              "text": ", press "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Add the preset's provider"
            },
            {
              "text": ", then paste your key on its row. For a server of your own, fill in a name and a base URL under "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Your own provider"
            },
            {
              "text": " instead: a server on this PC, or one on your home network by its private address, takes no key. Then press "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "List models"
            },
            {
              "text": "."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "On "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "AI › Self-test"
            },
            {
              "text": ", press "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Run self-test"
            },
            {
              "text": ". It takes a few seconds and works at the title screen too. Its verdict says whether replies will come quickly enough."
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "text": "Load your character. When Home's state reads "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Speaking"
            },
            {
              "text": ", walk up to one of the characters on Characters › Named NPCs. When you are close, a hint shows the talk key: press "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "V"
            },
            {
              "text": ", type your line and press "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Enter"
            },
            {
              "text": ". "
            },
            {
              "strong": true,
              "text": "Esc"
            },
            {
              "text": " closes the box."
            }
          ]
        ],
        "ordered": true
      },
      {
        "note": [
          {
            "strong": true,
            "text": "Note."
          },
          {
            "text": " Model calls wait until EldenNet has confirmed that you are offline and alone in your own world. While you play with others online, EldenNet pauses."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "If something goes wrong",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "text": "Home says what is wrong and what to do about it, and System › Status says it part by part. "
          },
          {
            "doc": "troubleshooting",
            "text": "Troubleshooting"
          },
          {
            "text": " explains every message."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "See also",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "paragraph": [
          {
            "doc": "keys",
            "text": "Keys and pad"
          },
          {
            "text": " · "
          },
          {
            "doc": "provider",
            "text": "What is sent to your provider"
          },
          {
            "text": " · "
          },
          {
            "doc": "privacy",
            "text": "Privacy"
          },
          {
            "text": " · "
          },
          {
            "doc": "writing-content",
            "text": "Writing content"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "Getting started"
  },
